OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["http://dx.doi.org/10.3758/s13421-022-01373-4"],"publicationDate":"2022-11-18","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":true,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::9f7b515ebb66207457455cfd9b6ab557","fullName":"Miyuki Nakamura","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-3395-3177"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Yujiro Kawata","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Yujiro Kawata","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Yujiro Kawata","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Masataka Hirosawa","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Tsuneyoshi Ota","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":6,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Tsuneyoshi Ota","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":7,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Tsuneyoshi Ota","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":8,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Nobuto Shibata","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":9,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"emotional memory"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"memory"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"sex differences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"exercise"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Sports and Active Living"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"05 social sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"GV557-1198.995"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0501 psychology and cognitive sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"cortisol"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Sports"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Differential effects of acute exercise on emotional memory in men and women","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Exercise may change emotional memory, which is associated with the induction of mental disorders such as depression and anxiety. This effect of exercise may be influenced by exercise-induced cortisol release. Depending on sex, cortisol exerts differential effects on emotional memory consolidation. However, whether acute exercise and exercise-induced cortisol release have sex-dependent effects on emotional memory has not been established. Therefore, first, we aimed to determine the effects of acute exercise on emotional memory, separately for men and women, in a within-subjects design. Second, we aimed to examine whether the effects of acute exercise on emotional memory are related to the effects of exercise-induced cortisol release, separately for men and women. Sixteen healthy men and 15 healthy women were presented with positive and negative emotional images, followed by either rest or a vigorous-intensity cycling exercise condition using a within-subjects design on separate days. Salivary cortisol was measured before presenting the emotional images presentation and 20 min after each intervention. Emotional memory was assessed two days later. Vigorous-intensity exercise decreased emotional memory in women, whereas there was no change in men after rest or exercise. Cortisol levels increased after exercise intervention in both men and women, although there was no association between cortisol levels and emotional memory. These findings demonstrate that the effect of a single bout of vigorous-intensity exercise on emotional memory differs between men and women and is associated with decreased emotional memory in women.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2023-05-10","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Front Sports Act Living","Frontiers in Sports and Active Living, Vol 5 (2023)"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Frontiers in Sports and Active Living","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2624-9367","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":null,"vol":"5","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::b68a86b6291eac9e313f66b3d30efb67","originalIds":["10.3389/fspor.2023.1062051","50|doiboost____|b68a86b6291eac9e313f66b3d30efb67","od_______267::42c478f52d262bd5dc1734f9210f7420","37234750","PMC10208400","50|od_______267::42c478f52d262bd5dc1734f9210f7420","oai:pubmedcentral.nih.gov:10208400","oai:doaj.org/article:d9d9fb42111740c18c949ebf9f39811c","50|doajarticles::dec0a27df84a1214b56e4d01a9e83d32"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3389/fspor.2023.1062051"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"37234750"},{"scheme":"pmc","value":"PMC10208400"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":5.0,"influence":2.2660032E-9,"popularity":4.8825446E-9,"impulse":5.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Juntendo University","acronym":"Juntendo University","id":"openorgs____::46ed57754533152e110898096c9076e2","pids":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"34077901"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000417622738"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/01692sz90"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.258269.2"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100005731"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q3244340"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"18069345"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q3244340"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100005731"}],"countries":[{"code":"JP","label":"Japan"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.juntendo.ac.jp/english/"},{"legalName":"Institute of Sports Medicine and Science","acronym":"Institute of Sports Medicine and Science","id":"pending_org_::fd29e88f75a205bcae4856d7572abd67","pids":[{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q11313173"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000406420014"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.510366.7"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/05jh42p10"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q11313173"}],"countries":[{"code":"JP","label":"Japan"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.sorc.or.jp/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"driver______::bee53aa31dc2cbb538c10c2b65fa5824","value":"DOAJ"},{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"},{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3389/fspor.2023.1062051"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.3389/fspor.2023.1062051"],"publicationDate":"2023-05-10","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::cb8d0357ffb3a538fefd1e72df511503","value":"Frontiers in Sports and Active Living"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"37234750"},{"scheme":"pmc","value":"PMC10208400"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3389/fspor.2023.1062051"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37234750"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::cb8d0357ffb3a538fefd1e72df511503","value":"Frontiers in Sports and Active Living"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3389/fspor.2023.1062051"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["http://dx.doi.org/10.3389/fspor.2023.1062051"],"publicationDate":"2023-05-10","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3389/fspor.2023.1062051"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doaj.org/article/d9d9fb42111740c18c949ebf9f39811c"],"publicationDate":"2023-05-01","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::cb8d0357ffb3a538fefd1e72df511503","value":"Frontiers in Sports and Active Living"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"driver______::bee53aa31dc2cbb538c10c2b65fa5824","value":"DOAJ"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":true,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::0ab9d4be151e398b7a2c3e0ccb468109","fullName":"Jennifer L. Etnier","name":"Jennifer L.","surname":"Etnier","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-3080-0565"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Jarod C. Vance","name":"Jarod C.","surname":"Vance","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Aiko Ueno","name":"Aiko","surname":"Ueno","rank":3,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"03 medical and health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0302 clinical medicine"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Effects of Acute Exercise on Memory Performance in Middle-Aged and Older Adults","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Numerous studies show that exercise benefits memory and some show that acute exercise prior to encoding has larger benefits than exercise after encoding. This study was designed to investigate the effects of acute exercise on memory in middle-aged and older adults (<jats:italic>M</jats:italic><jats:sub>age</jats:sub> = 64.71 years) and to explore the influence of the timing of the exercise on these effects. Using a within-subjects design, moderate-intensity exercise (20 min) was either not performed (control), performed before the task (exercise prior), or performed after the task (exercise post). Memory was assessed using the Rey Auditory Learning Verbal Test. For short- and long-term memory and learning, significantly more words were remembered in the exercise-prior condition than the others. For 24-hr recall, participants remembered significantly more words in the exercise-prior condition than exercise post, which was better than control. Exercise benefits memory for healthy middle-aged and older adults, with the greatest benefits when performed prior to encoding.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2021-10-01","publisher":"Human Kinetics","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":null,"container":{"name":"Journal of Aging and Physical Activity","issnPrinted":"1063-8652","issnOnline":"1543-267X","issnLinking":null,"ep":"760","iss":null,"sp":"753","vol":"29","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::5d2b87705c8c036ede1cbe46c59b1ac3","originalIds":["10.1123/japa.2020-0208","50|doiboost____|5d2b87705c8c036ede1cbe46c59b1ac3","3128795496"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1123/japa.2020-0208"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":6.0,"influence":2.3029703E-9,"popularity":5.136938E-9,"impulse":3.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":null,"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1123/japa.2020-0208"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1123/japa.2020-0208"],"publicationDate":"2021-10-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::2a42ba5ecd60d9a4ee26cebefcf76134","value":"Journal of Aging and Physical Activity"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3128795496"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1123/japa.2020-0208"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.1123/japa.2020-0208"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3128795496"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1123/japa.2020-0208"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.1123/japa.2020-0208"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"rui yang","name":"rui","surname":"yang","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0002-2317-8704"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"xiguang zhang","name":"xiguang","surname":"zhang","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"wenyi li","name":"wenyi","surname":"li","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"cheng guo","name":"cheng","surname":"guo","rank":4,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"hybrid","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"03 medical and health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0302 clinical medicine"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Treadnill exercise ameliorated stress-induced neuron impairment and dopamine loss in rat hippocampus and improved working memory","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Stress-related memory deficit is correlated with neurotransmitter system impairment. Exercise improves memory function and neurotransmitter. However, no studies have been performed to directly observe exercise-related effects on neurotransmitter in stress model, in association with memory function and hippocampal neuron. This study aimed to investigate the effect of exercise on hippocampal neuron and dopamine in stress model, followed by working memory in a passive avoid test. Our study found that stress rat had significantly neuron impairment and dopamine loss in hippocampus plus working memory deficit, which can be rescued by exercise. In summary, this study demonstrated that the neuroprotective effect of stress-associated working memory by treadmill exercise via ameliorated neuron impairment and dopamine loss.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2023-01-30","publisher":"Wiley","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::0f2b4c2b43559f64d109a46bbd3e8c3b","originalIds":["10.22541/au.167508632.24198391/v1","50|doiboost____|0f2b4c2b43559f64d109a46bbd3e8c3b","10.21203/rs.3.rs-3092984/v1","50|doiboost____|a346a4d7783caf7962c2689e6b56faf8"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.22541/au.167508632.24198391/v1"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.21203/rs.3.rs-3092984/v1"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":1.6835128E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Capital University of Physical Education and Sports","acronym":"Capital University of Physical Education and Sports","id":"openorgs____::ca1d070e362dd9f718c3f3b1ae3b3d88","pids":[{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.440659.a"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/054nkx469"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000405619208"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q15942570"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q15942570"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"https://www.cupes.edu.cn/"},{"legalName":"Beijing Sport University","acronym":"BSU","id":"openorgs____::29038f1f01f3765a0ca731c811f05dc8","pids":[{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.411614.7"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"7945999"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/03w0k0x36"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q3551745"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"87710204"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q3551745"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000122235394"}],"countries":[{"code":"CN","label":"China (People's Republic of)"}],"websiteurl":"http://en.bsu.edu.cn/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.22541/au.167508632.24198391/v1"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.22541/au.167508632.24198391/v1"],"publicationDate":"2023-01-30","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.21203/rs.3.rs-3092984/v1"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"hybrid"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-3092984/v1"],"publicationDate":"2023-07-05","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Zakary Patrick","name":"Zakary","surname":"Patrick","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Myungjin Jung","name":"Myungjin","surname":"Jung","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Terry McMorris","name":"Terry","surname":"McMorris","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Paul D. Loprinzi","name":"Paul D.","surname":"Loprinzi","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0001-7711-4741"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":"hybrid","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Male"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Adult"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Memory, Long-Term"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Time Factors"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Research"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"05 social sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Body Mass Index"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Young Adult"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Memory, Short-Term"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Mental Recall"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Humans"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0501 psychology and cognitive sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Female"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Exercise"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"The effects of acute exercise on memory: considerations for exercise duration and participant body mass index","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>           <jats:p>Acute moderate-intensity exercise has been demonstrated to improve memory performance. It is less clear, however, whether the duration of acute exercise and body mass index (BMI) may moderate this effect. Thus, the purpose of this experiment was to evaluate the effects of differing exercise durations (20- and 40-minutes) on immediate and long-term memory performance, while considering BMI as a moderating factor in this exercise duration and memory performance relationship. Twenty-three young healthy adults participated in a within-subjects experiment. Participants completed four different experimental visits including either exercising at a moderate intensity (or standing on a treadmill) for 20- or 40-minutes, followed by an immediate free-recall memory assessment and then a delayed 24-hr recall. Acute moderate-intensity exercise improved memory performance, regardless of the duration of exercise. Further, long-term memory performance was greater for individuals with a higher BMI when they engaged in shorter (20 min) exercise compared to longer (40 min) exercise.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2025-04-19","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media LLC","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Psychol Res"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Psychological Research","issnPrinted":"0340-0727","issnOnline":"1430-2772","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":null,"vol":"89","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::c150b141263378b9926a8e6c2e79da1e","originalIds":["2120","10.1007/s00426-025-02120-5","50|doiboost____|c150b141263378b9926a8e6c2e79da1e","od_______267::540524dcbab7f080aea6e2acccb96ce9","40252111","PMC12009224","50|od_______267::540524dcbab7f080aea6e2acccb96ce9","oai:pubmedcentral.nih.gov:12009224"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1007/s00426-025-02120-5"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"40252111"},{"scheme":"pmc","value":"PMC12009224"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":4.0,"influence":2.2772189E-9,"popularity":4.813093E-9,"impulse":4.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass